    [
     1,
     "Hello,\r<br>\r<br>The UK Breeding Bird Survey delivers satisfactory estimates from line\r<br>transect data with two intervals (truncated at 100 m).\r<br>\r<br>I am comparing some of my own line transect and point transect data,\r<br>both with two distance intervals.\r<br>\r<br>Is it a bad idea to attempt to estimate the detection function from\r<br>point transect data with just two distance intervals? I am seeing\r<br>overestimation for some species compared to the line transect density\r<br>results.\r<br>\r<br>I am using Distance 6.0 and assuming a half-normal model.\r<br>\r<br>Are there any published studies where point transects with two distance\r<br>intervals have produced satisfactory estimates?\r<br>\r<br>Stephen.\r<br>\r<br>--\r<br>distance-sampling list home page:\r<br>  <a href=\"http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477322212000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2rjLL6uAjQdZR9z7yMExGk\">http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html</a>\r<br>To unsubscribe, go to the home page and click &quot;Join or leave the list&quot;,\r<br>  or email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jisc...@jiscmail.ac.uk</a> with the following message body:\r<br>  leave distance-sampling\r<br>Before posting to the list, read the list guidelines at\r<br>  <a href=\"http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477322212000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2owTTbkYB8kj1yuJrK3W73\">http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/</a>\r<br>    distance-sampling.welcome\r<br>Any questions, email the list owner at\r<br>  <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance-sam...@jiscmail.ac.uk</a>\r<br>--\r<br>"
    ]
